{"id":240619536775136,"type":"genre","name":"Vaudeville","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":71,"info":{"img":null},"own_scenes":[{"id":61,"name":"Nostalgia de entreguerras: New Vaudeville Band y Bonzo Dog","book":{"id":1,"slug":"1966_Savage","title":"1966: The Year the Decade Exploded","author":"Jon Savage","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/1966/","families":{"beat":{"name":"Beat británico, mod y freakbeat","color":"#ef4444"},"garage":{"name":"Garage y punk americano","color":"#f97316"},"folk":{"name":"Folk rock y canción protesta","color":"#a3e635"},"psico":{"name":"Psicodelia, LSD y raga rock","color":"#c084fc"},"pop":{"name":"Pop de estudio: Spector, Beach Boys, Meek","color":"#38bdf8"},"soul":{"name":"Soul, Motown, R&B y ska","color":"#facc15"},"vanguardia":{"name":"Vanguardia: Warhol, Velvet, free jazz, arte","color":"#e5e7eb"},"juventud":{"name":"Juventud, moda y medios: Swinging London, radio pirata","color":"#f472b6"},"politica":{"name":"Política: CND, Vietnam, derechos civiles, feminismo, gays","color":"#22d3ee"}}},"family":"Pop de estudio: Spector, Beach Boys, Meek","color":"#38bdf8","start":1961,"end":1967,"place":"Londres","desc":"Mientras «Distant Drums» frenaba el pop británico en otoño, se abrió un túnel del tiempo. Geoff Stephens, excománager de Donovan harto de «discos fúnebres y deprimentes» de poetas y psicodelia, compró viejos 78 de los años veinte y escribió «Winchester Cathedral», cantada por John Carter a través de las manos como por un megáfono: número 4 en octubre y éxito en Estados Unidos. Como no había grupo, montó la New Vaudeville Band copiando el aspecto de la Bonzo Dog Doo-Dah Band, grupo de escuela de arte de Vivian Stanshall que versionaba canciones de entreguerras con sensibilidad dadaísta y máquinas autodestructivas; la copia obligó a los Bonzos a escribir lo suyo. Ese gusto por los años veinte venía de la Temperance Seven, los Alberts y la nostalgia de los Lovin’ Spoonful y de «Sunny Afternoon»: nostalgia accesible, casi camp. El pasado se convirtió en presente y futuro.","aka":["vaudeville","Twenties revival","vo-do-de-o","Bonzo Dog Doo-Dah Band"],"notes":[],"influences":[{"name":"El pop de papá y mamá","id":102596754039589,"type":"genre"},{"name":"CND y las marchas de Aldermaston","id":88507073182577,"type":"genre"}],"refs":[{"ch":11,"q":"It was as though a time tunnel had opened up in the swirls of pop modernism.","para":"It was as though a time tunnel had opened up in the swirls of pop modernism. Six places down from ‘Distant Drums’ in the 1 October chart was the debut record by a new group, the New Vaudeville Band. Beginning with a prolonged instrumental introduction, ‘Winchester Cathedral’ resolved into a Rudy Vallee-style vocal that cannily mixed the 1920s with the 1960s – nobody said ‘You’re bringing me down’ in the interwar period – before climaxing with a set of vo-do-de-o’s.","page":430,"pdf":283,"chapter":"Octubre: Winchester Cathedral: tiempo pasado, presente y futuro"},{"ch":11,"q":"Fronted by hooligan singer Vivian Stanshall, the Bonzo Dog Doo-Dah Band were an art-school group.","para":"Fronted by hooligan singer Vivian Stanshall, the Bonzo Dog Doo-Dah Band were an art-school group. Their love of obscure 1920s records was allied to a Dadaist sensibility: their name came from a random word cut-up and their stage shows were augmented by auto-destructive machines (Roger Ruskin Spear had been to Ealing Art School and, like Pete Townshend, had fallen under Gustav Metzger’s spell) and surreal props – word balloons, gorilla suits. To top it off, they wore baggy 1920s suits, short haircuts and co-respondent shoes – then the cutting edge of fashion.","page":433,"pdf":284,"chapter":"Octubre: Winchester Cathedral: tiempo pasado, presente y futuro"},{"ch":11,"q":"The hype had become real. The past had become the present and the future.","para":"In the short term, Geoff Stephens and the New Vaudeville Band had the last laugh. Later in the month, ‘Winchester Cathedral’ hit the Billboard Top 100 as the highest new entry. Under the firm tutelage of road manager Peter Grant, Tristram and the others went to America, where they played Las Vegas and appeared on the Ed Sullivan Show. Their success encouraged other musicians to try out versions of the 1920s style that had been the pop music of their parents’ youth. It became a mini-vogue. The hype had become real. The past had become the present and the future.","page":434,"pdf":285,"chapter":"Octubre: Winchester Cathedral: tiempo pasado, presente y futuro"}],"artists":[{"id":224700393071892,"type":"artist","name":"Herman's Hermits","rating":null},{"id":248686499240525,"type":"artist","name":"The Bonzo Dog Doo-Dah Band","rating":null},{"id":9389669148996,"type":"artist","name":"The New Vaudeville Band","rating":null},{"id":27741781912781,"type":"artist","name":"Vivian Stanshall","rating":null},{"id":49737607678135,"type":"artist","name":"The Temperance Seven","rating":null},{"id":191330147492833,"type":"artist","name":"John Carter","rating":null},{"id":98444379464066,"type":"artist","name":"The Alberts","rating":null},{"id":246530849624916,"type":"artist","name":"Neil Innes","rating":null},{"id":48023393818723,"type":"artist","name":"Alan Klein","rating":null},{"id":51435764648542,"type":"artist","name":"Dave Berry","rating":null},{"id":136041894023975,"type":"artist","name":"The Roaring 60s","rating":null},{"id":224075159838535,"type":"artist","name":"Spike Milligan","rating":null},{"id":259114979210758,"type":"artist","name":"Spencer’s Washboard Kings","rating":null},{"id":42602969657157,"type":"artist","name":"Legs Larry Smith","rating":null},{"id":64195513758118,"type":"artist","name":"Rodney Slater","rating":null},{"id":193013064604131,"type":"artist","name":"Geoff Stephens","rating":null},{"id":220849946319925,"type":"artist","name":"Bob Kerr","rating":null},{"id":245406810235823,"type":"artist","name":"Peter Grant","rating":null}],"tracks":[{"id":136686595480272,"artist_id":98444379464066,"artist":"Th